        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Wichita, Sedgwick County, Kansas, United States\n- Buildings: Wichita City Carnegie Library Building\n- Organizations/Registers: National Register of Historic Places\n- Concepts: Carnegie libraries, county seats\n\nFacts:\n- The Wichita City Carnegie Library Building is a Carnegie library at 220 S. Main Street in Wichita, Sedgwick County, Kansas, United States.\n- The Wichita City Carnegie Library Building was built in 1915.\n- The Wichita City Carnegie Library Building was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1987.\n- Wichita is the county seat of Sedgwick County, Kansas.\n- Wichita is the most populous city in Kansas.",
